WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.820
The saxophone was
invented in the mid 1800s

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:05.730
by Adolphe Sax, the son
of Belgium's chief

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:06.930
instrument maker.

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:10.140
With the saxophone, sax
blended the power of a

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:12.840
brass horn with the
nuances of a woodwind

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.450
instrument. This was an
instrument that could

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.300
sound bright and edgy or
dark and moody.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:20.850
It's no wonder the
saxophone has found a

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:24.600
place in many music
styles, from jazz to pop

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:25.800
to the classics.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:31.670
The standard saxophone
has 23 different tone

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:34.250
holes and an equal
number of key cups to

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:37.520
close them. At this
factory, each key cup is

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:38.780
assembled by hand.

